1. Conditional Statement

Definition:
A conditional statement is used to make a decision in a program based
 on whether a condition is true or false.


2. if Statement

Definition:
The if statement 
executes a block of code only when the given condition is true.



3. if-else Statement

Definition:
The if-else statement executes one block when the condition is true 
and another block when the condition is false.




4. else-if Ladder

Definition:
An else-if ladder is used to check multiple conditions one by one
. The block of the first true condition is executed.

5. Nested if

Definition:
A nested if is an if statement inside another if statement.


6. switch Statement

Definition:
The switch statement is used to select one option
 from multiple choices based on the value of an expression.


 7. Conditional Operator ?:

Definition:
The conditional operator is a short form of if-else.
 It is also called the ternary operator because it uses three operands.

Syntax:

condition ? expression1 : expression2;